From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bsps/microblaze: re-enable linker relaxation

Reverts "bsps/microblaze: Disable linker relaxation".  That patch added
-Wl,--no-relax to work around a binutils bug: the MicroBlaze relaxation pass
corrupted the addend of R_MICROBLAZE_64 relocations with a non-zero addend,
silently miscompiling RTEMS at -O2 (see ANALYSIS.md).

The binutils fix landed upstream on 2026-08-13 ("ld: microblaze: don't index
the local symbol cache with a global symbol index"); it is in binutils master
and kept here under patches/binutils/landed/0001.  With a toolchain that
carries it, relaxation is safe again, so drop the workaround and let GCC's
default -relax run -- relaxation trims redundant IMM instructions and recovers
the ~520 bytes of text the workaround cost.

REQUIRES the RTEMS MicroBlaze toolchain to be built with a binutils that has
the fix.  The RTEMS 6/7 toolchain uses the Xilinx binutils 2.36.1 snapshot,
which does NOT; apply this only after that binutils is updated or the fix is
backported, otherwise the silent miscompile returns.  Once relaxation is back
on, the BSPs pinned to -O0 for this bug (bspkcu105 et al., which link
../../opto0) can also return to -O2.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/spec/build/bsps/microblaze/microblaze_fpga/abi.yml b/spec/build/bsps/microblaze/microblaze_fpga/abi.yml
--- a/spec/build/bsps/microblaze/microblaze_fpga/abi.yml
+++ b/spec/build/bsps/microblaze/microblaze_fpga/abi.yml
@@ -13,30 +13,8 @@ default:
   - -mno-xl-soft-div
   - -mno-xl-soft-mul
   - -Wl,-EL
-  - -Wl,--no-relax
 description: |
-  ABI flags.
-
-  The MicroBlaze GCC link spec passes -relax unconditionally.  Linker
-  relaxation deletes redundant IMM instructions, and while doing so it
-  corrupts the addend of R_MICROBLAZE_64 relocations which have a non-zero
-  addend: the addend loses four bytes for each IMM deleted ahead of the
-  relocation.  Relocations with a zero addend in the same section resolve
-  correctly, so this is silent - there is no link error, just a load from
-  the wrong address.
-
-  A structure member reference such as
-
-    lwi rD, r0, _Per_CPU_Information + offsetof(Per_CPU_Control, executing)
-
-  therefore reads the preceding member instead.  RTEMS then hands out the
-  wrong executing thread, which breaks resource ownership and thread
-  identity throughout the system.  It shows up with optimization enabled
-  and is largely hidden at -O0, which is why these BSPs were built at -O0.
-
-  -Wl,--no-relax overrides the -relax from the link spec.  Observed with
-  binutils 2.36.1; it also removes the intermittent ld segmentation faults
-  seen when linking the testsuite.
+  ABI flags
 enabled-by: true
 links: []
 name: ABI_FLAGS
